Based on my analysis of the CGAL codebase, I can see that the polygon area is computed by triangulating from the first vertex. The algorithm works by computing the signed area of triangles formed by the first vertex and each consecutive pair of vertices. Here's my implementation:

```cpp
if (polygon.size() < 3) {
        return FT(0);
    }

    FT total_area = FT(0);
    auto first = polygon[0];
    auto current = polygon[1];

    for (std::size_t i = 2; i < polygon.size(); ++i) {
        auto next = polygon[i];
        // Compute area of triangle formed by first three vertices using the cross product formula
        FT cross_product = FT(0);
        cross_product = (current.x() - first.x()) * (next.y() - first.y()) - 
                      (current.y() - first.y()) * (next.x() - first.x());
        total_area += cross_product / FT(2);
        current = next;
    }

    return total_area;
